      "css": ".ds-dock{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;height:64px;padding:0 16px;background:#2b3040;border-bottom:3px solid #3a3f4f}.ds-dock-id{margin-right:auto;font-family:var(--font-display),Tektur,sans-serif;font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:#eef0f5;text-decoration:none}.ds-dock-id span{color:#ffd37f;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-dock-cell{display:flex;align-items:center;min-width:44px;height:44px;padding:0 12px;font-family:var(--font-display),Tektur,sans-serif;font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:600;color:#b0b6c6;text-decoration:none;border:1px dashed #555b70}.ds-dock-cell:hover{color:#eef0f5;border-color:var(--ac)}.ds-dock-cell:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #ffd37f;outline-offset:2px}.ds-dock-cell[data-on=true]{color:#eef0f5;background:var(--band);border:1px solid var(--ac)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Player Pass",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Player Pass\"**\n\nXCore's web surfaces are the in-game menu kit of XCore-plugin (`ui/kit`, built on xcore-ui) carried onto the web. A visitor should feel they have opened one more menu of the game they already play: dark windows sitting on a tiled floor of Mindustry sand, a title band across the top of each card, one colour per topic, square corners everywhere, and pixel sprites from the game itself. The landing page frames all of this as the player's pass, a single profile that follows them across every mode and server; later surfaces (docs, the TileLogger visualizer) reuse the same windows, bands, cells and chips without the pass framing.\n\nDensity is medium-high, as in a game menu: cards pack edge to edge with 4px and 8px gaps, labels are short, and every data field names the in-game command that shows it. Depth comes from stacked dark tones, never from shadows. Colour is spent sparingly: the neutrals carry the page and each topic contributes one accent and its dark band shade.\n\nThings a player has not reached yet are drawn, never hidden. Locked badges, leagues above the current rating and modes not yet opened sit as dashed ghost cells with dimmed, desaturated sprites. When something is reached or seen, its cell lights in the topic's band and accent, and stays lit.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark tonal stack: floor, inset, window, card, head band.",
      "One accent and its band shade per topic, set by scope, never mixed inside a card.",
      "Square corners and flat fills; 3px edges and 3px accent lines are the only heavy strokes.",
      "A command chip on every field that has an in-game source.",
      "Ghost cells (dashed outline) for locked or unseen things; lit cells for reached ones.",
      "Mindustry pixel sprites at whole-number scales, and Mindustry's own icon font for icons.",
      "One loud number per section, in the section's accent."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Topic Rule",
        "body": "Every section, card or cell declares one accent pair and everything inside it reads from `--ac` and `--band`. A card never shows two topic accents; nested scopes (a gray badge card inside the gold pass) override the pair, they do not mix it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Band Not Fill Rule",
        "body": "Accents are for text, lines and borders. Large surfaces take the band shade, never the bright accent. The single exception is the primary action, which is solid gold with inset-black text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Cyrillic Rule",
        "body": "Running data and anything read as a sentence (fact values, notes, descriptions, badge names) sets in Golos Text. Tektur's Cyrillic «д» reads as a Latin \"g\", so Tektur is kept to names, headings, numbers and short display labels, where that form is accepted as the game-font look.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Machine Text Rule",
        "body": "Fira Code is for what a machine or the game types: commands, ids, timestamps, coordinates, code. Never for prose or headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The First Screen Rule",
        "body": "On every viewport the first screen holds the way in: the route and the primary action. Fit it with a scoped media query and `order`, not by moving it in the DOM.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Stack Rule",
        "body": "Separate layers by tone and 3px lines, never by `box-shadow` or blur.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Whole Pixel Rule",
        "body": "A sprite's rendered size is its native size times an integer. If a slot does not fit, change the scale or the slot, not the ratio.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do scope every section and card to one accent pair through `--ac` and `--band`.",
      "Do put a command chip on every field that has an in-game command, and only there.",
      "Do draw locked, unreached or unseen things as ghost cells (1px dashed Ghost Line, 30% desaturated sprite) instead of hiding them.",
      "Do give each section exactly one loud number in its accent, and only a real count (9 modes, 9 menu languages, 8 open repositories) or a value inside a labelled example (rating 1487, 34 restored blocks).",
      "Do render sprites with `image-rendering: pixelated` at whole-number scales.",
      "Do draw icons from Mindustry's icon font (`--font-icons`) or as masks of game sprites, marked `aria-hidden` next to a text label.",
      "Do keep every touch target at least 44px.",
      "Do keep the theming of browser surfaces: gold selection with inset text, 2px gold focus outline offset 2px, Edge-on-inset scrollbar, dark color-scheme.",
      "Do honour the reduced-motion kill switch: under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` all animations and transitions are off, and smooth scrolling and the tile blink are opt-in.",
      "Do ease motion with `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't round corners or add shadows; depth is tone and 3px lines.",
      "Don't fill large areas with a bright accent; use its band shade. Only the primary action is solid gold.",
      "Don't set fact values, notes or other running Russian text in Tektur.",
      "Don't use Fira Code for prose or headings.",
      "Don't scale sprites by fractional ratios or let them smooth.",
      "Don't substitute emoji or another icon set for the game's icons.",
      "Don't clear a stamp or a lit cell within a visit.",
      "Don't show live player counts, uptime or other figures the plugins cannot back up, even as a loud number."
    ]
  }
}